-- Written by AI on 2026-10-17 by Claude Opus 5.5 (where-was-i cut v9), from Resolve 21.1's stock
-- "Word Highlight" subtitle template (Templates.drfx, Edit/Titles/Subtitles/Animated). Josh's look
-- 2026-10-16-signpost-pill: A's type (Futura Bold, white, the size of 80 px type in a 1080 px wide frame)
-- with B's orange pill (#D9531E, fully rounded) behind the word being spoken, centred at y 1470 of a
-- 1080x1920 frame (Fusion y 0.234375, from the bottom).
-- Colours: Fusion titles work in the timeline's scene-linear space. In a DaVinci WG/Intermediate timeline
-- with Rec.709 Gamma 2.4 output and the DaVinci DRT, the pill values are #D9531E converted from Rec.709 to
-- DaVinci Wide Gamut linear the way the graphics' colour node converts: (0.44925, 0.15145, 0.09010), which rendered
-- as exactly (217, 83, 30) on 22 Oct. The 17 Oct values (0.7492, 0.1648, 0.0923) rendered as (255, 69, 0) on the
-- pipeline's timelines, which use the inverse DRT; fixed 22 Oct by Claude Fable 5.1 from the director's arithmetic.
-- Pill height -0.012 and offset Y -0.003 (22 Oct, Claude Fable 5.1): the pill now covers descenders (g, y) with a
-- 4 px margin; at -0.018 the tail of a y poked out of the pill's curved end (the first codex-switch run, fault 50).
-- The highlighted word keeps white text through "Highlight Fill" (on, white).
-- Install: copy into ~/Library/Application Support/Blackmagic Design/DaVinci Resolve/Fusion/Templates/Edit/Titles/,
-- restart Resolve, then slowly drag it onto a subtitle track header.
{
